The report generation process is optimized for both memory and CPU usage, considering the large dataset generated by the network health monitoring. It generates detailed reports, including the frequency of each hostname, average latency, and individual check metrics (start time, end time, success/failure status, and latency), with a focus on minimizing latency and maximizing throughput.

The architecture takes into account potential external service downtimes, network fluctuations, and variable latency spikes, requiring developers to implement adaptive algorithms to maintain stability and reliability. The solution also considers the integration of third-party logging services, ensuring compatibility and minimizing overhead.

Overall, this code provides a scalable and efficient solution for network health monitoring, balancing performance and resource usage under high-load conditions.']

