The function then enters a loop that simulates real-time data acquisition by setting the value of each node's timestamp and sensor reading. The timestamps are incremented sequentially starting from the current time, and the sensor readings are generated within a specified range. Lower and upper bounds for this range should be provided as parameters.

The function also implements memory management and concurrency handling using appropriate synchronization mechanisms when interacting with the external memory pool manager and managing concurrent access to shared resources without causing data corruption. It provides robust error handling for all memory operations, ensuring that any allocation failures are managed gracefully by freeing any allocated resources before returning an error status.

The function also provides a mechanism to report the current memory usage statistics, including total allocated memory, free memory, and memory pool utilization, after the function execution. This will help in monitoring the efficiency of memory management and identifying potential bottlenecks.

Finally, the function implements a function to traverse the linked list and calculate the average sensor reading over a specified time window. The time window should be defined by the user and should be validated for correctness. This will assist in analyzing trends and making informed decisions based on the sensor data.

