The function is designed to be thread-safe by using a mutex lock around the memory allocation and deallocation operations. This ensures that multiple threads can access the memory pool manager safely without interfering with each other.

The function also includes a wrapper function `threadSafeDynamicMemoryManagement` that provides a thread-safe interface to the dynamic memory management function. This wrapper function takes the same arguments as the original function, but it uses a mutex lock around the call to the original function to ensure that it is thread-safe.

The function also includes a logging system that records all memory allocation and deallocation events. This allows for detailed logs of the memory usage and performance of the function, which can be useful for debugging and performance analysis.']

