The function first initializes a semaphore with a unique name and supports both increment and decrement operations using the `init_semaphore` function. It then dynamically allocates memory for an array of long integers to store the offsets of each record, an array of int integers to store the keys of each record, and an array of struct record objects to store the records read from the stream. The function reads the stream and stores the numbers in the dynamically allocated arrays, freeing the memory allocated for the arrays of long integers and int integers after storing the numbers.

The function then finds the smallest number in the array and prints it along with its offset using a helper function that calculates the median of all numbers in the array and prints it along with its offset. The function also frees the memory allocated for the array of struct record objects before closing the semaphore.

