The program creates a vector of tasks to execute and spawns them concurrently using the `tokio` runtime. It then waits for all tasks to complete and logs any errors that occur during task execution. The program also sets up signal handling to gracefully shut down when it receives a SIGINT signal.

The program uses a custom error type to encapsulate both descriptive strings and numerical error codes, which allows it to handle various types of errors in a consistent manner. It also implements a flexible logging mechanism that records detailed messages to a rolling log file, ensuring that each log entry includes a timestamp, task name, and error code if an asynchronous task fails. The program uses `snprintf` and `va_start/va_end` within asynchronous functions to format log messages efficiently.

