The code also includes a mutex to ensure thread-safety during concurrent access to the task collection. It uses the `pthread_mutex_lock()` and `pthread_mutex_unlock()` functions to acquire and release the lock on the mutex, respectively.

The code also includes error handling mechanisms to handle insufficient memory allocation gracefully. If there is not enough capacity for a new task, it reallocates the memory for the tasks array to double its size. It also checks if the index of the task to be removed is valid before attempting to remove it.

